{"id":"1671326b9da9e4e8cfa6015e4a175f18","name":"test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread[True]","start":1794843332083,"stop":1794843332187,"duration":104,"status":"passed","fullName":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register#test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread","retryHash":"3b8b4af1a7ac9dec8847283961634708.8ee89f01f3f42a039f3321f8d56d17b0","testCaseHash":"3b8b4af1a7ac9dec8847283961634708","parametersHash":"8ee89f01f3f42a039f3321f8d56d17b0","environmentHash":null,"flaky":false,"muted":false,"known":false,"isRetry":false,"labels":[{"name":"tag","value":"asyncio"},{"name":"parentSuite","value":"tests.unit_tests"},{"name":"suite","value":"test_bg_job_register"},{"name":"host","value":"runnervm8axu0"},{"name":"thread","value":"3662-MainThread"},{"name":"framework","value":"pytest"},{"name":"language","value":"cpython3"},{"name":"package","value":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register"}],"groupedLabels":{"tag":["asyncio"],"parentSuite":["tests.unit_tests"],"suite":["test_bg_job_register"],"host":["runnervm8axu0"],"thread":["3662-MainThread"],"framework":["pytest"],"language":["cpython3"],"package":["tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register"]},"parameters":[{"name":"from_threadpool","value":"True","hidden":false,"excluded":false,"masked":false}],"links":[],"steps":[{"link":{"id":"d57538f7eeda588b5602468251c5181b","originalFileName":"dd49de4e-7f3b-4e3d-99b1-f5687af5002a-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","name":"log","contentType":"text/plain","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":201},"type":"attachment"}],"error":{},"testCase":{"id":"3b8b4af1a7ac9dec8847283961634708","externalId":"b26b2803a1572059e3c99b23587b1127","name":"test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread[True]","fullName":"tests.unit_tests.test_bg_job_register#test_ws_poll_info_receives_terminal_status_from_worker_thread"},"descriptionHtml":"<p>A job finishing in its worker thread must wake the WS waiter in the main loop.</p>\n<pre><code>``run_command`` runs the job in a separate thread with its own event loop, but\nthe ``new_log_evt`` waiters live in the daemon loop. ``asyncio.Event.set()`` is\nnot thread-safe, so without hopping back onto the daemon loop the terminal DONE\nnotification is lost and ``ws_poll_info`` hangs forever (the desktop app's\n&quot;finalizing&quot; step never completes and the connection eventually drops).\n``from_threadpool`` mimics sync routes (``/update/start``), which call\n``run_command`` from FastAPI's threadpool, with no running loop.\n</code></pre>\n","environment":"default","setup":[{"id":"2827ab95e54ead7ba117fccf45625432","type":"before","name":"event_loop_policy","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"8e485d9eb95e72d531934c134a9b81ca","type":"before","name":"tmp_path_factory","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"8b08c55eacd89b89305b06fb55496fde","type":"before","name":"_isolated_hf_credentials","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":1},{"id":"0a8bb8107325e348b774e447a97f937f","type":"before","name":"_no_telemetry","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"8924f5797f812024bbf766b97624a7e7","type":"before","name":"monkeypatch","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0},{"id":"413196486c4ca92e0e260be356aecd05","type":"before","name":"_function_scoped_runner","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0}],"teardown":[{"id":"f9cd298188f7973513e44bbe57068ddf","type":"after","name":"_function_scoped_runner::0","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":1},{"id":"e8421a3d1d98cd78a101ffefcc1af665","type":"after","name":"monkeypatch::0","status":"passed","steps":[],"duration":0}],"history":[],"retries":[],"breadcrumbs":[["tests.unit_tests","test_bg_job_register"]],"retry":false,"transition":"new","titlePath":["tests","unit_tests","test_bg_job_register.py"],"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"attachments":[{"link":{"id":"d57538f7eeda588b5602468251c5181b","originalFileName":"dd49de4e-7f3b-4e3d-99b1-f5687af5002a-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","name":"log","c